title: The Church – A Called Out Assembly of Believers
description: The church as the called out assembly of believers from Abel to today: the church in the wilderness, entering the house of God, Christ the foundation, local independent New Testament churches, pastors and deacons, the two ordinances, and not forsaking the assembling together.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-church.html

# One deck for the whole of studies/data/topics/church.json, each theme given the same weight, framed as the
# author asked: the called out assembly of believers from Adam through today, the congregation in the wilderness,
# the people entering into the house of God, and the local independent churches of the New Testament and today.
# Also drawn from: 12266 and 16841 (a line of faith since Abel), 8757 (Hebrews 12), 10435, 15610, 15167, 17754,
# and the Exodus 33 and Revelation 1-3 studies (10373, 15406-15442).
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.

=== A called out assembly
--- The Church [title]
overline: Doctrine · The church
heading: A Called Out Assembly of Believers
sub: The church Christ founded, the pastor, and assembling together.
refs: Matthew 16:18; Acts 7:38; 1 Timothy 3:15; Hebrews 10:25
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 15408
--- What a church is
lead: Church is a called out assembly of believers. The people of God are required to come when called together. This was true in the OT and it is true in the New.
p: “A church is not a place it's a people!” So true, but the people need a place to gather, and having one fixed location and time makes that possible.
p: *For where two or three are gathered together in my name, there am I in the midst of them.* Wonderful promise of the Lord. This presupposes you are actually gathering.
refs: Matthew 18:20; Judges 21:8-10

=== From Abel to today
# from 12266
--- A line of believers stretching back to Adam
kicker: From Abel to today
lead: I am a saved Christian. Born again by the faith that was shared to me by another saved Christian, who in turn believed and was converted by yet another saved Christian. A line of succession going back to the beginning of the world.
p: A line of believers stretching back to Adam. To Abel. To Seth and Enos. The same faith of Abraham who believed the Lord and it was counted unto him for righteousness. The same faith that makes up the record of the “Hall of faith,” in Hebrews chapter 11.
big: Genesis 4:26 | mark: then began men to call upon the name of the LORD

# from 16841
--- Before Abraham, before the law
kicker: From Abel to today
p: The idea of the worship of God originating with Abraham, and only his seed after the flesh, is incorrect. There were many following the flood and the dispersion of nations out from Babel, that called upon the name of the Lord for salvation.
p: We see the greatest man on Earth at this moment, according to God, Job, who feared Him, eschewing evil, offering sacrifices to sanctify himself and his family. Without the law. Without the temple. Without a priesthood.
take: Salvation has always been by grace alone through faith in the Lord, calling upon his name. And that salvation was always offered to all people.
refs: Job 1:1; Job 1:5; Hebrews 11:4

# from 7254
--- Bethel, the house of God
kicker: From Abel to today
scripture: Genesis 28:16-17 | mark: this is none other but the house of God
p: Jacob stacks the rocks he'd slept on into a pillar, and anoints it with oil, renaming the place Bethel. This is the first time we see the concept of a house of God. And he vows to give the tenth unto the Lord.
big: 1 Timothy 3:15 | mark: the house of God, which is the church of the living God, the pillar and ground of the truth

# from 8757
--- The general assembly and church of the firstborn
kicker: From Abel to today
scripture: Hebrews 12:22-24 | mark: To the general assembly and church of the firstborn, which are written in heaven
p: We aren't under the covenant of Sinai, but of Zion. We are of the new covenant of a Heavenly Zion, which established life, in the continued presence of the Lord.
read: app:doctrine-salvation~12266 | A trail of blood of believers
read: app:doctrine-salvation~16841 | Job: faith in God before Abraham
read: app:doctrine-church~7254 | Bethel, the pillar and the house of God
read: app:doctrine-law~8757 | Not Sinai but Mount Sion

=== The church in the wilderness
# from 10372
--- The church in the wilderness
kicker: The church in the wilderness
big: Acts 7:38 | mark: the church in the wilderness
p: Stephen calls Israel gathered under Moses at Sinai *the church in the wilderness*, who *received the lively oracles to give unto us.*

# from 10373
--- The Tabernacle of the congregation
kicker: The church in the wilderness
scripture: Exodus 33:7 | mark: called it the Tabernacle of the congregation; every one which sought the LORD went out unto the tabernacle of the congregation
p: The Tabernacle without the camp, the church in the wilderness. This is the representation of the local church, the gathering of the congregation of those seeking the Lord. It represents both spiritual separation, and the physical assembly of believers that is our community church.
p: This is the pattern God showed Moses, and the pattern He gives us throughout the NT in the epistles. Local, independent churches that have fellowship in the Lord.

# from 12424
--- Every Levite given his charge
kicker: The church in the wilderness
p: **Numbers 4** sees God lay out the calling to each family of the Levites for ministering to the Tabernacle. And each man of each clan given a role, specific to them. With the whole given to the purpose of God.
p: Just as today, we who are saved are given different ways to be ministers of the faith and to edify the church, carrying that which is holy forth, into the world. Whatever you are called to contribute, do with cheer that the church may grow, and move out into the wilderness bringing others to Christ.

# from 12432, 12553
--- Without the camp
kicker: The church in the wilderness
p: The unclean were put without the camp that their uncleanliness doesn't affect others. Physically they are instructions to keep diseases from spreading. Spiritually, all are a picture of sin, and the exile similar to church discipline, the removal of leaven that can spoil a whole lump.
p: Even today, in our churches, there are those that give a bad report, who sow discord among the brethren. We are called to a different spirit, like Caleb. Don't be a burden or a stumbling block for others in church. Be a blessing. Seek to build.
refs: Numbers 5:2-3; Numbers 14:24; Proverbs 6:19
read: app:Exodus-33 | Exodus 33: the Tabernacle of the congregation
read: app:doctrine-church~12424 | Every Levite given his charge
read: app:doctrine-church~12553 | God hates them that sow discord

=== Entering into the house of God
# from 16757
--- Standing for the reading of the Word
kicker: Entering into the house of God
scripture: Nehemiah 8:5-6 | mark: and when he opened it, all the people stood up
p: Here is the tradition we Baptists have, of standing out of respect for God's word as the man of God preaches from the pulpit.
p: This is the purpose of the called out assembly. To give understanding to the people, reading from the Law of God distinctly. Notice the people were outside. They made booths of branches. It was simple and about God and His word.

# from 9125
--- As His custom was
kicker: Entering into the house of God
big: Luke 4:16 | mark: as his custom was, he went into the synagogue on the sabbath day
p: In these times, synagogues were the local churches of those who worshipped God. And Luke tells us that going to these houses of worship was Jesus' custom. It was His routine.
p: I am sure Jesus Christ Himself sat through boring sermons, by dull preachers who were wrong on doctrine, in congregations of people who were sinners and hypocrites or holier than thous. But it was Jesus' custom. And so, to begin His work, Jesus went to church. We should too.

# from 15215, 16492
--- He entered not into the temple
kicker: Entering into the house of God
big: 2 Chronicles 27:2 | mark: howbeit he entered not into the temple of the LORD
p: Jotham did that which is right in the sight of the Lord, but he did not enter into the temple. And the people were yet corrupt. How much more had he done had he not forsaken the assembly. If he had gone to church?
big: Haggai 1:9 | mark: Because of mine house that is waste, and ye run every man unto his own house
p: How relevant a verse for us today, where there are empty churches, dying congregations of senior saints, and no young people there building the local church up.

# from 17754, 15167
--- In the midst of the congregation
kicker: Entering into the house of God
big: Psalm 22:22 | mark: in the midst of the congregation will I praise thee
p: We cannot lift up our voice in praise to the congregation, to declare His name unto the brethren, if we avoid church.
p: When the armies of Ammon and Moab assemble against Jerusalem, Jehoshaphat calls the people together. A called out assembly in fast, and prayer, and singing songs in praise of God. Calling on Him to remember His promise, showing they have faith in His word.
refs: 2 Chronicles 20:4; 2 Chronicles 20:21-22
